# Regression lock for #105 r2 review-REFUTED defect 1 (cross-module bare-name
# type collision): a module declaring `Payload{a,b:int32}`. Paired with
# fnsig105_r2_collision_mody.cheng, which declares a STRUCTURALLY UNRELATED
# `Payload{text:str}` under the same bare name in a different module. A
# fn(...)-typed formal parameter declared against THIS Payload must reject a
# callback declared against the OTHER Payload -- comparing declared types by
# their trailing dotted component alone (the r1-REFUTED behavior) cannot
# tell these apart, since both strip to the bare name "Payload".
type
    Payload =
        a: int32
        b: int32
